"""
Standard class glider, 15 m span.

The fuselage `Body` is the free-flying base: it owns the position and the
quaternion orientation states and is *not* attached to the world by any
joint. Everything else hangs off its `frame_a`, whose axes are x forward,
y up, z to the right, matching the world frame convention.

# The datum is the centre of gravity

`fuselage.frame_a` is the aircraft datum, and the fuselage mass is placed
so that the *composite* centre of gravity of the whole aircraft falls
exactly on it: `r_cm_fuselage` is computed from the surface masses and
their stations rather than being set by hand. This is what ballast does on
a real glider, and it is what makes `x_ac_wing` mean "wing aerodynamic
centre ahead of the centre of gravity" --- the quantity that sets the
static margin --- instead of "ahead of an arbitrary reference point".

Change a surface mass or station and the fuselage mass moves to rebalance,
so the static margin stays the property of the aerodynamic geometry alone.

# Inertia axes

In this frame roll is about x, **yaw is about y** and **pitch is about z**,
so the diagonal inertia entries map as `I_11 = roll`, `I_22 = yaw`,
`I_33 = pitch`. The values are quoted about the fuselage's own centre of
mass, which is where `Body` expects them; the parallel axis shift to the
datum is done by `Body` from `r_cm`.
"""
component Glider
  "Density and wind"
  air = AirState()
  "Elevator deflection, positive trailing edge down, which pitches the nose down"
  elevator = RealInput() if has_htail
  fuselage = MultibodyComponents.Body(m = m_fuselage, r_cm = r_cm_fuselage, I_11 = I_fus_roll, I_22 = I_fus_yaw, I_33 = I_fus_pitch, orientation_state = MultibodyComponents.OrientationState.Quaternion(), statePriority = 1000, linearStatePriority = 1000, initialize_orientation = false, r_0(initial = r_start), v_0(initial = v_start), Q_hat(initial = q_start))
  wing = Wing(b = b_wing, S = S_wing, x_ac = x_ac_wing, y_ac = y_ac_wing, dihedral = dihedral_wing, incidence = incidence_wing, m = m_wing, CL0 = 0.25, CL_alpha = 5.7, CD0 = 0.008, CM0 = -0.09, e_oswald = 0.95, alpha_stall = 0.244)
  fus_mount = MultibodyComponents.FixedTranslation(r = [x_cp_fuselage, 0.0, 0.0], render = false)
  fus_drag = DragBody(CdA_x = CdA_fus_x, CdA_y = CdA_fus_y, CdA_z = CdA_fus_z)
  htail = Wing(has_control = true, b = b_htail, S = S_htail, x_ac = x_ac_htail, y_ac = y_ac_htail, dihedral = 0.0, incidence = incidence_htail, m = m_htail, I_panel = 2.0, CL0 = 0.0, CL_alpha = 4.4, CD0 = 0.008, CM0 = 0.0, e_oswald = 0.85, alpha_stall = 0.244, CL_delta = CL_delta_elev, CM_delta = -0.55, CD_delta = 0.02) if has_htail
  "Fit a horizontal tail; false leaves the aircraft pitch unstable on purpose"
  structural parameter has_htail::Boolean = true
  # --- fuselage -------------------------------------------------------------
  "Mass of the fuselage, including the pilot and everything not in a surface"
  parameter m_fuselage::Mass = 230.0
  "Fuselage roll inertia about its own centre of mass"
  parameter I_fus_roll::Inertia = 35.0
  "Fuselage yaw inertia about its own centre of mass"
  parameter I_fus_yaw::Inertia = 700.0
  "Fuselage pitch inertia about its own centre of mass"
  parameter I_fus_pitch::Inertia = 700.0
  # --- launch condition -----------------------------------------------------
  """
  Launch state, given the way a flight condition is actually quoted: a
  speed, a flight path angle and a pitch attitude. The incidence follows as
  `theta_start - gamma_start`. The defaults are the hand-computed trim of
  the rig below; a residual here simply excites the phugoid.
  """
  parameter r_start::Position[3] = [0.0, 500.0, 0.0]
  "Airspeed at release"
  parameter V_start::Velocity = 25.0
  "Flight path angle at release, negative descending"
  parameter gamma_start::Angle = -0.0235
  "Pitch attitude at release, positive nose up"
  parameter theta_start::Angle = 0.0257

  "Initial velocity of the datum, world frame"
  final parameter v_start::Velocity[3] =
      [V_start * cos(gamma_start), V_start * sin(gamma_start), 0.0]
  "Initial attitude quaternion [w,i,j,k]; pitch is a rotation about the body z axis"
  final parameter q_start::Real[4] =
      [cos(theta_start / 2), 0.0, 0.0, sin(theta_start / 2)]
  # --- wing -----------------------------------------------------------------
  "Wing span"
  parameter b_wing::Length = 15.0
  "Wing area"
  parameter S_wing::Area = 10.5
  """
  Wing aerodynamic centre ahead of the centre of gravity. This is the static
  margin knob: because the datum is the centre of gravity, moving the wing
  aerodynamic centre forward is the same as moving the centre of gravity aft,
  and the neutral point follows at about 0.9 times the change. Trimmed at
  0.205 m the aircraft sits near 18% MAC, in the usual sailplane band.
  """
  parameter x_ac_wing::Length = 0.205
  "Wing aerodynamic centre above the centre of gravity"
  parameter y_ac_wing::Length = 0.0
  "Wing dihedral"
  parameter dihedral_wing::Angle = 0.052
  "Wing incidence relative to the fuselage datum, so the fuselage flies near zero incidence"
  parameter incidence_wing::Angle = 0.05236
  "Wing mass"
  parameter m_wing::Mass = 100.0
  # --- horizontal tail ------------------------------------------------------
  "Tailplane span"
  parameter b_htail::Length = 2.2
  "Tailplane area"
  parameter S_htail::Area = 1.0
  "Tailplane aerodynamic centre ahead of the centre of gravity; negative is aft"
  parameter x_ac_htail::Length = -4.0
  "Tailplane aerodynamic centre above the centre of gravity"
  parameter y_ac_htail::Length = 0.25
  """
  Tailplane incidence relative to the fuselage datum. This is the rigging
  angle that sets the trim speed: the wing's camber moment `CM0` is
  nose-down and has to be balanced by a download on the tail, so the
  tailplane is set at a negative incidence. With it at zero the aircraft
  still trims, but at a useless incidence of about -2 degrees, and dives
  away at 90 m/s.
  """
  parameter incidence_htail::Angle = -0.037373
  "Tailplane mass"
  parameter m_htail::Mass = 12.0
  "Tailplane lift coefficient per radian of elevator deflection"
  parameter CL_delta_elev::Real = 2.2

  # --- fuselage aerodynamics ------------------------------------------------
  """
  Station of the fuselage drag point, ahead of the centre of gravity. Slender
  body theory puts the body's normal force about a quarter of the body length
  behind the nose, which for this fuselage is just ahead of the centre of
  gravity; that is what produces the fuselage's destabilising contribution to
  pitch and yaw, so the station matters more than the drag areas do.
  """
  parameter x_cp_fuselage::Length = 0.225
  "Fuselage axial drag area Cd*S; the equivalent flat plate area of a clean glider"
  parameter CdA_fus_x::Area = 0.05
  "Fuselage normal drag area Cd*S, from the plan area and a slender-body cross-flow Cd"
  parameter CdA_fus_y::Area = 2.1
  "Fuselage side drag area Cd*S, from the side area and a slender-body cross-flow Cd"
  parameter CdA_fus_z::Area = 2.4
  "Spanwise station of the wing panels"
  final parameter y_panel_wing::Length = b_wing / (2 * sqrt(3.0))
  "Height of the wing mass above the datum"
  final parameter y_cm_wing::Length = y_ac_wing + y_panel_wing * sin(dihedral_wing)
  "Mass of the tailplane actually fitted"
  final parameter m_htail_fitted::Mass = ifelse(has_htail, m_htail, 0.0)
  "Total aircraft mass"
  final parameter m_total::Mass = m_fuselage + m_wing + m_htail_fitted
  """
  Fuselage centre of mass relative to the datum, chosen so that the
  composite centre of gravity of the aircraft lands on the datum.
  """
  final parameter r_cm_fuselage::Position[3] = -(m_wing * [x_ac_wing, y_cm_wing, 0.0] + m_htail_fitted * [x_ac_htail, y_ac_htail, 0.0]) / m_fuselage
relations
  connect(fuselage.frame_a, wing.frame_a)
  connect(air, wing.air)
  connect(fuselage.frame_a, fus_mount.frame_a)
  connect(fus_mount.frame_b, fus_drag.frame_a)
  connect(air, fus_drag.air)
  if has_htail
    connect(fuselage.frame_a, htail.frame_a)
    connect(air, htail.air)
    connect(elevator, htail.delta_l, htail.delta_r)
  end
end

"""
Free flight with the wing only, released level.

With no tailplane the wing lift acts ahead of the centre of gravity, so
`dCm/dalpha` has the wrong sign and the aircraft has no pitch stiffness:
the expected result is a monotone pitch departure, not a glide. This is the
increment that proves the tail is what stabilises the aircraft rather than
some artefact of the assembly.
"""
test component TestGliderWingOnly
  world = MultibodyComponents.World()
  atm = Atmosphere(rho0 = 1.225)
  glider = Glider(has_htail = false)
relations
  connect(atm.air, glider.air)
end

"""
Free flight with wing and tailplane, released level with the elevator
neutral.

The aircraft now has pitch stiffness, so instead of departing it should
converge onto a glide, oscillating on the way in the slow, lightly damped
phugoid mode whose period is close to `pi*sqrt(2)*V/g`.
"""
test component TestGliderTailed
  world = MultibodyComponents.World()
  atm = Atmosphere(rho0 = 1.225)
  glider = Glider()
  elev = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = 0.0)
relations
  connect(atm.air, glider.air)
  connect(elev.y, glider.elevator)
end